WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.570
Hi.

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.830
My name is Olivia Yao.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.900
I'm a senior studying
mechanical engineering

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.310
and human-centered design.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.900
And I'm currently
the editor-in-chief

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.250
of Infinite Magazine.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.620
Infinite Magazine is the
student-run art and fashion

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.828
magazine on campus.

00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:13.620
We really want to
provide a creative outlet

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.745
for all of our students
studying technical studies.

00:00:15.745 --> 00:00:19.000
In addition, we're a place for
people to explore and have fun.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.220
I'm Hamilton Forsythe.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.130
I'm a junior.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.910
I'm studying arts and design,
which is in the architecture

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:24.480
department.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.190
I would say the
mission statement

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.350
is to give a voice
to the people who

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.330
feel like they're
underrepresented here

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:34.380
at MIT, which directly relates
to fashion, and design,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.300
and culture, and
how we integrate

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.090
those things with
technology here at MIT.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.750
I think coming out
of high school,

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.030
I was trying to find some way to
explore myself and explore who

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.780
I was as an individual,
and fashion really

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.920
allowed me to do that.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.670
So the magazine has a bunch
of different ideas categorized

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.420
into spreads.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.490
And each spread starts
with a student idea.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.060
So a student will
come and approach

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.500
saying I want explore this
topic in my visual spread.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.528
And we help the iterate
and refine that idea

00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:02.820
into something that could be
presentable in a magazine.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.580
From there, we help them secure
materials and secure models.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.650
We have photo shoots
and then we have people

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.780
lay the spread out in InDesign.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.130
It's a great balance between
group and individual work.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.800
As a busy MIT student,
you know you can't do

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.900
every aspect of every design.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.790
And you might not
even have the skills

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.705
to do those things as well.

00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:25.080
I think the most interesting
project that Infinite's ever

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.300
done is the launch box that we
did last issue for our launch

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:28.800
event.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.500
We created a 10 foot
by 10 foot room.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.940
It was bodega style.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.820
It was an interactive art
exhibit of pages and images

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.570
from the magazine.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.520
And people could walk
in, take pictures,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.740
explore the magazine
in a physical sense,

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.495
instead of just
flipping through pages.

00:01:42.495 --> 00:01:44.640
The launch from last
semester was something

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.370
that I've contributed the most
to and felt the most proud of.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.460
Being able to actually
come up with that idea

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.640
and build the launch box
from scratch on my own,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.030
makes it really,
really important to me.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.040
The Infinite community
is pretty special to me.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.450
It's a lively group of people.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.340
But what makes it
special is that we're all

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.063
interested in
growing creatively,

00:02:04.063 --> 00:02:06.480
and we're all really supportive
of each other's individual

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.830
projects.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.110
I definitely want to
keep expanding Infinite,

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:13.530
making it more
visible not only MIT,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.480
but I also want to
start reaching out

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.250
into the Boston area.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.530
And put MIT on
the map as a place

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.000
to be for fashion and design.

